      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[St George's Hospital]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[Opening Hours and Cover: Mon - Fri 08:30 - 17:00 - Telephone and/or Email referral for Emergency and same week referrals<br>Mon - Fri 17:00 - 08:30 - Telephone for ocular emergencies<br>Sat, Sun, BH - 08:30 - 21:00 - Telephone and/or Email referral for Emergency and same week referrals<br>Sat, Sun, BH - 21:00 - 08:30 Out of hours - Telephone for ocular emergencies<br><br>How to refer:<br>Please note that walk-ins/self-referrals are NOT accepted. <br> <br>Please complete the referral form below and email it to moorfields.sghurgentcare@nhs.net <br> <br>https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-elgkdhc4HZhoZgRA0iTwOlYIAN8vO0Z/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104561831344168348650&rtpof=true&sd=true<br><br>(Click File > Download > Microsoft Word)<br> <br>The referrals will be triaged within 4 hours during working hours, and the patient will be contacted directly to arrange a review if needed (please do not ask the patient to just turn up). <br> <br>If your referral is urgent, please call the triage line and send an e-referral form as above. <br><br>08:30-21:00 Mon-Sun - 02077025542<br>21:00 - 08:30 Night nurse triage - 07921056594<br><br><br>If a patient is seen at Kingston, St Heliers, Epsom or Croydon Hospitals out of hours, refer to St George's via telephone and email if ocular emergency. Refer via local pathways for other cases.<br><br>CUES<br>For patients with non-urgent sight or life-threatening conditions (e.g. red eye or eyelids, flashes and floaters (more than 72 hours*), dry, gritty and uncomfortable eyes, sticky discharge or watery eye, foreign body sensation in the eye) who are registered with a GP in Merton/Wandsworth, Richmond and Kingston, please refer to one of the participating high street opticians https://www.primaryeyecare.co.uk/find-a-practice/<br><br>Telephone: See above<br>Email: moorfields.sghurgentcare@nhs.net]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1643-F57C00-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Opening Hours and Cover">
            <value><![CDATA[Mon - Fri 08:30 - 17:00 - Telephone and/or Email referral for Emergency and same week referrals
Mon - Fri 17:00 - 08:30 - Telephone for ocular emergencies
Sat, Sun, BH - 08:30 - 21:00 - Telephone and/or Email referral for Emergency and same week referrals
Sat, Sun, BH - 21:00 - 08:30 Out of hours - Telephone for ocular emergencies

How to refer:
Please note that walk-ins/self-referrals are NOT accepted. 
 
Please complete the referral form below and email it to moorfields.sghurgentcare@nhs.net 
 
https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-elgkdhc4HZhoZgRA0iTwOlYIAN8vO0Z/edit?usp=sharing&ouid=104561831344168348650&rtpof=true&sd=true

(Click File > Download > Microsoft Word)
 
The referrals will be triaged within 4 hours during working hours, and the patient will be contacted directly to arrange a review if needed (please do not ask the patient to just turn up). 
 
If your referral is urgent, please call the triage line and send an e-referral form as above. 

08:30-21:00 Mon-Sun - 02077025542
21:00 - 08:30 Night nurse triage - 07921056594


If a patient is seen at Kingston, St Heliers, Epsom or Croydon Hospitals out of hours, refer to St George's via telephone and email if ocular emergency. Refer via local pathways for other cases.

CUES
For patients with non-urgent sight or life-threatening conditions (e.g. red eye or eyelids, flashes and floaters (more than 72 hours*), dry, gritty and uncomfortable eyes, sticky discharge or watery eye, foreign body sensation in the eye) who are registered with a GP in Merton/Wandsworth, Richmond and Kingston, please refer to one of the participating high street opticians https://www.primaryeyecare.co.uk/find-a-practice/
]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Telephone">
            <value>See above</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Email">
            <value>moorfields.sghurgentcare@nhs.net</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
