      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[St Thomas' Hospital]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[Opening Hours and Cover: 08.30-16:00<br><br>Patients can self-refer via telephone during opening hours by calling 020 7188 4336 and will receive a triage call from one of our clinicians, within an hour, to advise appropriate next steps.<br><br>Referrers should call 020 7188 4336 and will be transferred to a clinician to discuss referral. Once accepted, inform patient to attend the Rapid Access Eye Clinic (Ground Floor, St Thomas' Hospital South Wing) with referral letter.<br><br> <br><br>Out of hours - ophthalmologist on call available for advice via switchboard.<br><br> <br><br>Out of hours – patient should attend general A&E if true emergency.<br>Telephone: 020 7188 4336 (triage and referral advice in hours)<br><br>020 7188 7188 (switchboard)<br>Email: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1643-F57C00-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Opening Hours and Cover">
            <value><![CDATA[08.30-16:00

Patients can self-refer via telephone during opening hours by calling 020 7188 4336 and will receive a triage call from one of our clinicians, within an hour, to advise appropriate next steps.

Referrers should call 020 7188 4336 and will be transferred to a clinician to discuss referral. Once accepted, inform patient to attend the Rapid Access Eye Clinic (Ground Floor, St Thomas' Hospital South Wing) with referral letter.

 

Out of hours - ophthalmologist on call available for advice via switchboard.

 

Out of hours – patient should attend general A&E if true emergency.]]></value>
